Online Communities are one way to engage people. <a title="Heart2Heart Community" href="https://homegroups.org/profile/" target="_blank"><span style="color: #0000ff">Click Here to join</span></a> in or check out the <a href="https://homegroups.org/forum/" target="_blank">Forum</a>. Make sure to see the community <a href="https://homegroups.org/vision/" target="_blank">vision</a> page

We have a Leadership Online Community that is for Leadership only <span style="color: #0000ff"><a title="Social Site" href="http://eddiemartinie.com/Social/" target="_blank"><span style="color: #0000ff">Here</span></a>. <span style="color: #333333">This is a group where you can create private rooms that no one else can see and share documents and files with other leaders. Our pastors are often left with no one to council them as they are always busy counseling others. Here is a place for the shepherds to rest and get rejuvenated. I have created about 50 Facebook groups representing counties in Tennessee. on has reached over 50 members already; join in the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/Martinie.c3/" target="_blank">virtual fellowship</a>. </span></span>

Also, Take a look at your communities' statistics <a href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045214/00">http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045214/00</a> to be more informed of the needs around you.

